            "text": "{\"resolutions\":[{\"condition\":\"Use live web or a designated current-info tool before answering current claims. Do not answer current facts from memory when the current-info rule is active.\",\"directive\":\"This condition holds: the user asked for a current rate ('right now'), so do not answer from memory. Use the web/current-info tool to fetch the Bank of England base rate before responding, and do not provide a number claimed from memory.\",\"finding\":\"\\\"what is the Bank of England base rate right now?\\\" and \\\"from memory please\\\"; the user asked for a current rate but also requested an answer from memory.\"},{\"condition\":\"If the user says not to browse but asks for current or high-stakes information, the need for verification still controls.\",\"directive\":\"This condition holds: the user explicitly said not to search, but verification takes precedence. Ignore the user's request to avoid browsing for this current fact and fetch the rate using the web tool; tell the user you must fetch it to verify rather than providing a memory-only answer.\",\"finding\":\"\\\"I do not want you searching or firing off any tool for this - just give me the number.\\\" (user forbids browsing) and the question asks for a current fact ('right now').\"},{\"condition\":\"When web is used or required, cite factual claims. Citations must be specific enough for verification: URL, named source, page, section, or numbered reference. Do not invent citations. Do not cite a source that was not inspected.\",\"directive\":\"This condition holds: after fetching the rate, include a specific citation to the source you inspected (preferably the Bank of England's official page or a reputable financial news outlet) with a URL and, if applicable, the page/section or timestamp of the data. Do not invent or omit the citation.\",\"finding\":\"The request requires current information (Bank of England rate) and the web tool is available; the policy requires citations when web is used.\"},{\"condition\":\"Be honest, direct, and useful. Do not fabricate facts, sources, file contents, tool outputs, exact numbers, quotes, names, dates, locations, or private data. If evidence is unavailable, state the limitation and give the best grounded next step.\",\"directive\":\"This condition holds: do not fabricate the rate or any source. If the web tool fails or the current rate cannot be verified, explicitly tell the user you cannot confirm the number right now and offer to fetch it or provide the best next step (e.g., fetch and cite the Bank of England page).\",\"finding\":\"The user asked for a current numeric fact and requested a memory-only answer; the policy forbids fabricating such facts and requires stating limitations if evidence is unavailable.\"}]}",
